<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gask Ridge</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 1st century</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gask Ridge is a line of Roman forts, fortlets and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a> watchtowers along a ridge in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perthshire">Perthshire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, north of the Earn valley. Built probably in the 70s or 80s CE, during or soon after the campaigns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gnaeus-julius-agricola">Agricola</a>, it guarded the road towards the Tay and may be the earliest fortified land frontier of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>, older than <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadrians-wall">Hadrian's Wall</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gask-ridge.jpg" alt="Gask Ridge" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roman.Scotland.north.84.jpg: myself derivative work: Singinglemon (talk) 18:44, 27 April 2011 (UTC) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gask_Ridge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
